Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:24:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test(steps): exercise the keyed click in the entry flow

The keyed click had no scenario, only unit coverage of its guard. This walks
the same main-menu path the label-based scenario walks, by key instead, so a
green pair means the two spell the same journey. This one also passes on a
game running in another language, which is the point of the step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Pickle/Features/entry-flow.feature | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Pickle/Features/entry-flow.feature b/Pickle/Features/entry-flow.feature
index 950e6d2..dca9f71 100644
--- a/Pickle/Features/entry-flow.feature
+++ b/Pickle/Features/entry-flow.feature
@@ -12,3 +12,10 @@ Feature: entry flow
     Then window "Page_SelectStoryteller" is open
     When I click button "Back"
     Then window "Page_SelectScenario" is open
+
+  Scenario: a button answers to the key its label came from
+    Given the main menu is open
+    When I click button keyed "NewColony"
+    Then window "Page_SelectScenario" is open
+    When I click button keyed "Next"
+    Then window "Page_SelectStoryteller" is open
